{"content":[{"c":["GERSHOM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Moses’ son by Zipporah, born in Midian during Moses’ exile from Egypt (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.2.22","r":"Exod.2.22","rawR":"Exod.2.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.2.22","value":"Exod.2.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 2:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.18.3","r":"Exod.18.3","rawR":"Exod.18.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.18.3","value":"Exod.18.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"18:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.23.15-16","r":"1Chr.23.15-16","rawR":"1Chr.23.15-16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.23.15-16","value":"1Chr.23.15-16"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 23:15-16"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Jonathan’s father. He and his sons were priests to Dan’s tribe. The Danites set up a graven image to worship and appointed Jonathan to be their priest (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.18.30","r":"Judg.18.30","rawR":"Judg.18.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.18.30","value":"Judg.18.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 18:30"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Alternate spelling of Gershon, Levi’s oldest son (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.1,16-17,20,43","r":"1Chr.6.1,16-17,20,43","rawR":"1Chr.6.1,16-17,20,43","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.1,16-17,20,43","value":"1Chr.6.1,16-17,20,43"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:1, 16-17, 20, 43"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.23.6-7","r":"1Chr.23.6-7","rawR":"1Chr.23.6-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.23.6-7","value":"1Chr.23.6-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"23:6-7"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=GershonGershonites_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"GershonGershonites_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"GershonGershonites_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Gershon, Gershonites"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Ancestor of Shebuel, the chief officer over the temple treasury during David’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.26.24","r":"1Chr.26.24","rawR":"1Chr.26.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.26.24","value":"1Chr.26.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 26:24"},")."],"sourceCla